  "slug": "codes-topic-f271",
  "summary": "Six preprints apply constraint solving, tree search, LLM-driven search and verified compilation to cut circuit cost across error-correction and algorithm layers.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is automated, search-based design of quantum circuits under explicit cost or correctness constraints. For fault tolerance, Block Checks with Pareto tree search target depth-operation trade-offs in state preparation, while CP-SAT synthesis exploits code structure to lower logical error rates in syndrome extraction for CSS quantum LDPC codes. At the algorithm level, LLM-driven search redesigns the approximate RNS modular exponentiation pipeline for RSA-2048, reducing expected Toffoli count by up to 78.6%. QBlue is extended to block-encoding algorithms with machine-checked verification, evaluated on 279 programs against PennyLane. Structure-aware compilation for independent-set optimization and context-aware variational synthesis with mid-circuit reconstruction complete the picture. The novelty lies in coupling optimization with structural or formal guarantees, though the preprints address different circuit classes.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-26"
}
